This Collection Consists of a Group of Black and White Photographs (From The Late 19th Century) Showing Black People in A Variety of Activities Such AS Playing Cricket, Dancing, Singing, Autody A Slave Auction, Standing At A Railroad Station in Louisiana, Meeting Friends At A Ball, Dancing Under The Stars in Stars in Stars in In New Orleans Graveyard, Dancing in Front of a Bonfire, Gathering Herbs for Making Medicinal Folk Remedies, Attention Church on Sunday Morns, Listening to a female only soprano at Union Square in New York City; Serving As Well As Ding Farm Work; Attention to Funeral; Walking Down The Aisle During the Wedding Ceremony; Visiting Friends; Participating in Community Celebrations Such As Mardi Gras; and playing games. Notably Excluded Are Photographs of Black Entertainers Such As Minstrel Shows.

